   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) are differentiable, with \\( f(1) = -2 \\), \\( f'(1) = 6 \\), \\( g(1) = -1 \\), \\( g'(1) = 1 \\). Let \\( h(x) = f(x)g(x) - 3f(x) \\). Find the value of \\( h'(1) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -26
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( x = 1 \\): \\( f(1) = -2 \\), \\( f'(1) = 6 \\), \\( g(1) = -1 \\), \\( g'(1) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 6
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( (fg)'(1) = f'(1)g(1) + f(1)g'(1) \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( (6)(-1) + (-2)(1) = -8 \\).",
         "mathjson": -8
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The term \\( -3f(x) \\) contributes \\( -3f'(1) = -18 \\), so \\( h'(1) = -8 + (-18) = -26 \\).",
         "mathjson": -26
      }
   ],
